% Load phases (inputs share package scope; do not collect them at the top):
%
% 1. Package defaults, imports and initialization/early font metrics.
% 2. PDF layer setup, preliminary language, utilities and book defaults.
% 3. PDF color profile, typography and final common visual policy.
% 4. Front matter, song helpers, prose, media, melody, song metadata, notes and
%    repeats; repeats loads spacing policy and its Lua shipout owner in place.
% 5. Runtime installation and default index declarations, always last.
% See ARCHITECTURE.md for dependencies, state ownership and lifecycle conventions.
%
% Consumer overrides: for a providecommand default, define it before loading
% ulsbs with \providecommand (or \newcommand), or use \renewcommand afterward
% if its value is read at use time. Load-time options/measurements cannot be
% changed retroactively. For allocated dimensions/skips use \setlength after
% loading; assign count registers directly (e.g. \ulBreakPenalty=50\relax).
% Public booleans use setters, e.g. \ulShowTags{false}, and real predicates,
% e.g. \ifulShowTags ...\else ...\fi; do not redefine the predicates.


